# Data conversion between kilobyte and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kilobyte and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KB to 0.0009MiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0014MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 1048.576KB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 1572.864KB.

>>> source
const forward_whole: int = 1KB
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
const forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
const backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(KB))
const backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(KB))

<<< stdout
0.0009MiB
0.0014MiB
1048.576KB
1572.864KB

<<< stderr
